WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 28 Student Video
Unit 7, Lesson 4: Hell

1
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:13.900
Not long ago, I was speaking at a student conference, and afterwards, a young man

2
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.940
came up to me who was deeply troubled about the idea of hell.

3
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:23.360
He just couldn't reconcile that a loving God would send a good person to hell.

4
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.920
I did my best to answer his questions.

5
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.200
We talked probably 30-40 minutes, and it dawned on me.

6
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.520
His problem was he viewed people as being essentially good.

7
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.660
He kind of looked at God as if God is looking down and if someone does the slightest

8
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:40.720
small thing, that person goes to hell for eternity.

9
00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:46.020
He viewed it as if there's a few really bad people like Hitler out there but the

10
00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:51.420
rest of us are essentially good and so hell seemed like total overkill.

11
00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.340
Although it might surprise you, I actually agree with him in the sense that it would

12
00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:01.760
be total overkill for God to send a good person to hell.

13
00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:07.740
but the problem is the Bible has a very different view of human nature in

14
00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:13.080
Romans chapter 3 Paul says that no one is righteous no one is good

15
00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:18.940
all have turned away from God and in Mark chapter 7 Jesus says it is the

16
00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:24.760
heart that has fallen the heart is corrupt God doesn't send good people to hell

17
00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:26.940
because no one is good

18
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.780
History also supports this theological claim.

19
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:37.880
GK Chesterton once said that original sin, the brokenness of mankind is

20
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:42.900
the one doctrine that can be proven outside of the Bible and I think he's right.

21
00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:48.240
All we have to do is look at the history of mankind and it's clear that something is

22
00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.760
desperately broken with human beings.

23
00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:51.640
A

24
00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.700
colleague of mine Dr. Clay Jones has studied human evil and suffering as much as

25
00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:03.740
anybody who's alive. And to avoid the claim that his critics would make that he took

26
00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:09.480
the easy way out, he decided to study evil in depth in the 20th

27
00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:14.700
century. And he began with the assumption that evil was done by just a few deranged

28
00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.380
individuals. But what he found stunned him.

29
00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:23.040
What he found that it wasn't just the Pol Pots and the Hitlers that contributed to

30
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:28.540
evil but masses of human beings under the right circumstances and the right times

31
00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:34.400
did and practiced great acts of evil what he found was that human

32
00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.560
beings are deeply wicked

33
00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:42.400
let's look at just a few examples from the 20th century take the chinese government

34
00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:48.200
for example responsible for at least the deaths of 25 to 30 million

35
00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:53.760
people take the russians responsible for starving out at least 6

36
00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:59.520
million Ukrainians. And the Japanese government brutalized at least 300,000

37
00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:05.320
Chinese in what's called the Rape of Nanjing in a way that even Nazis

38
00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:11.000
looking on were horrified. Let's face it, in American culture, tens of millions

39
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.480
of abortions and even the practice of eugenics.

40
00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:19.780
The point is that mass evil is not done by individuals.

41
00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:22.940
But what Dr. Jones found, I think is right.

42
00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.960
Human beings are desperately corrupt.

43
00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:31.940
We are deeply fallen. God doesn't send good people to hell because nobody

44
00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:37.580
is truly good. When evil things happen, we often hear people describe it

45
00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:42.260
as inhumane. My father taught me when I was younger, he'd say, son, don't describe

46
00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:46.660
acts like that as inhumane because inhumane means not human.

47
00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.160
He'd say, son it's humans who do that.

48
00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:55.120
And he's right. Whether we turn on the daily news or we look throughout the history

49
00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:00.880
of the world, it's human beings who have done and continue to do evil things.

50
00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:08.080
You might be thinking okay okay so nobody is truly good but why

51
00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:13.300
would God send anybody to hell? Part of the answer is that God doesn't send

52
00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:19.040
people to hell. If C.S. Lewis was right in his classic book, The Great Divorce, God

53
00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.060
doesn't send people to hell. People choose it.

54
00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:26.440
In fact, towards the end of that book he famously says in the end there's two kinds

55
00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:32.260
of people, those whom say to God, thy will be done and those to whom God says,

56
00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.680
thy will be done. All who are in hell choose it.

57
00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:43.600
I have a good friend who's clinging to a particular sin in his life And I'll never

58
00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:49.260
forget when he once told me that he would not stop practicing this sin, even if it

59
00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:52.200
meant that God would condemn him to hell for eternity.

60
00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:58.040
There's a well-known atheist who died recently and he passed around news for

61
00:04:58.040 --> 00:04:59.580
everybody shortly before his death.

62
00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:04.220
He said, if any story comes out after I die that I converted on my bedside, that

63
00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:08.040
story is false. I will not believe in God.

64
00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.840
Friends, human autonomy is strong.

65
00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:15.560
God has given us free will and we are stubborn.

66
00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:21.580
Many of us don't want to believe in God and all that it entails to follow after him,

67
00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:25.460
but you know what? God is a respecter of persons.

68
00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:31.640
If people choose not to believe in God, God is not going to force them to believe

69
00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:37.420
in Him. Please realize the existence of hell brings no pleasure

70
00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:43.220
to God medieval depictions of people being tortured mercilessly and

71
00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:48.860
endlessly and somehow God reveling in this with pleasure are false hell

72
00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:54.240
is a terrible place we have been designed to be in a relationship with God and

73
00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:58.660
relationship with other people and in hell all of that is lost.

74
00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:02.760
But in Ezekiel 18 verse 23, God asks this.

75
00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:06.900
He says, do I have any pleasure in the death of the wicked?

76
00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:11.580
Would I not rather that they turn from their wicked ways and live?

77
00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.240
You might be wondering, well, why can't God just forgive?

78
00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:20.200
If God can do anything, can't he just announce that we're forgiven?

79
00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:25.860
Well, yes, God can do anything, but he can do anything consistent with his moral

80
00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:31.600
nature. God is the holy righteous judge of the universe therefore

81
00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:37.520
he can't be indifferent to sin but what God has done is even better you

82
00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:42.800
see he's offered the death of his son Jesus Christ who lived a perfect

83
00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:48.760
sinless life as an act of love towards us but also as an

84
00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:54.540
act of justice so the question is are we willing to accept the free offer

85
00:06:54.540 --> 00:07:00.320
of salvation, the free offer of forgiveness that God has to offer to each

86
00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:01.620
one of us.

87
00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.980
Let's face it, hell is a troubling thought.

88
00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:11.860
I don't like the idea of hell. The thought that some of my friends or family, loved

89
00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:16.800
ones or really anybody could end up in hell is a disturbing thought.

90
00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:21.740
When it's all said and done, to me there's one compelling reason to believe

91
00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:27.100
that hell is real. Jesus taught about the reality of hell.

92
00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:32.300
And Jesus had the most authority and clarity of vision of anybody who's ever lived.

93
00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:38.360
As a sinless son of God who performed miracles and rose from the grave, Jesus had

94
00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:40.220
the authority to teach about hell.

95
00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:45.200
If Jesus was willing to talk about it and warn people lovingly about the

96
00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:48.500
possibility of hell. How could we do any differently?

